  "text": "Recipe: Jowar Bowls\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Bowls\nIngredients: jowar flour (sorghum flour), boiled water, cashew powder, mango powder, sesame seeds, turmeric powder, asafoetida (hing), black pepper, garlic powder, cumin seeds\nCooking methods: bake, no-cook\nInstructions: Mix all the ingredients to prepare dough.\nAdjust water and flour to prepare dough with right consistency. If required, 1 or 2 tsp of additional water may be added.\nMake small balls with the dough. Then shape them into bowls with our hands or use silicon moulds.\nTransfer them to a baking dish lined with parchment paper. Bake at 180 C for 20 to 25 minutes.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (sorghum flour), NUTS & SEEDS (cashew powder), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
